Title: Jack and the Beanstalk
Credit: A pantomime by
Author: An OpenAct sample script
Draft date: Rehearsal draft

> ACT ONE <

.SCENE 1: THE VILLAGE OF LITTLE MOO
[[openact: full stage]]

A sunny village green: bunting, a well, and a sign reading LITTLE MOO, TWINNED WITH NOWHERE IN PARTICULAR. The VILLAGERS are mid-dance.

!SONG 1: MORNING IN LITTLE MOO (VILLAGERS)
[[openact: song | singers: VILLAGERS | function: Opening number: the village, and its money troubles | staging: Full company; DAISY the cow makes a late, hopeful entrance | feel: Bright and brassy]]

.SCENE 2: A LANE OUTSIDE THE VILLAGE
[[openact: front cloth]]

Tabs in. SILLY BILLY bounds on, waving at everyone.

SILLY BILLY
Hiya, boys and girls!

The audience reply.

SILLY BILLY
Oh, that was rubbish. My nan shouts louder than that, and she lives in Spain. When I say "Hiya, boys and girls", you shout "Hiya, Billy!" Ready? Hiya, boys and girls!

The audience shout back, louder.

SILLY BILLY
That's more like it. Now, Mum's sent me to market to sell Daisy the cow. But Daisy's my best friend. So I've got a plan.
(Leaning in)
I'm going to sell her very, very slowly.

DAME TROTT sweeps on in a dress made entirely of tea towels.

DAME TROTT
Billy! Have you sold that cow yet?

SILLY BILLY
Not yet, Mum. I've been making friends.

DAME TROTT
(To the audience)
Ooh, look at you all. Hello, darlings! I'm Dame Trott. I'd shake your hands, but I've just done my nails, and the varnish cost more than the cow.
[[Local gag option: swap the varnish line for the price of parking in town.]]

FLESHCREEP slides on behind them, rubbing his hands. The audience boo.

DAME TROTT
What's all that booing? Is it the dress?

SILLY BILLY
I think there's someone behind us, Mum.

DAME TROTT
Behind us? Don't be daft.
(To the audience)
Is there someone behind us?

The audience shout "He's behind you!" They turn one way; FLESHCREEP ducks the other. They try again, faster. And again.

FLESHCREEP
(Aside)
Enjoy your little lane, peasants. By tonight the Giant will own every cow, every crumb and every tea towel in this village.

DAME TROTT
Did somebody say tea towels?

FLESHCREEP exits with a swirl of his cloak, to boos.

!SONG 2: SELL HER SLOWLY (SILLY BILLY, DAME TROTT)
[[openact: song | singers: SILLY BILLY, DAME TROTT | function: Comic duet: Billy's plan to keep Daisy | staging: Front cloth; DAISY joins for the last chorus | feel: Music-hall patter song]]

~We'll sell her slowly, sell her slow,
~Down the lane and round we go,
~And if a buyer comes our way,
~We'll take the long way home today!

They exit, with DAISY trotting after. Tabs out.

.SCENE 3: THE MARKET SQUARE
[[openact: full stage]]

Stalls, striped awnings and a bustling crowd. FAIRY MOONBEAM enters stage right, as good fairies always do.

FAIRY MOONBEAM
In every tale, however tall, the smallest bean can save us all.

.SCENE 4: THE GIANT'S KITCHEN
[[openact: full stage]]

A table the size of a bus. A spoon the size of a canoe. FLESHCREEP polishes an enormous fork.

